<title>SOUTH KOREA: Cho Hung to set up subsidiary in Moscow.</title>
<headline>Cho Hung to set up subsidiary in Moscow.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Cho Hung Bank said on Tuesday it would set up a wholly owned subsidiary in Moscow in the second half of 1997 to expand business in Russia.</p>
<p>The bank said in a statement the subsidiary would be capitalised at $7 million.</p>
<p>A bank official said Cho Hung would be the first South Korean bank to set up a subsidiary in Moscow.</p>
<p>He said business would be focused on giving loans to South Korean companies operating in Russia.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5645</p>
